  {
   "id": "b2",
   "function": "problem",
   "scene_type": "zlx_cutaway",
   "spoken": "One working cycle is four strokes. For that, the crankshaft turns twice, a full seven hundred and twenty degrees. Only then does the next cycle begin. The bar at the bottom shows where we are right now. That is four strokes for every two turns of the crank.",
